 of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-upper-unconditional"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-upper-unconditional"],"id":"long.prop-upper-unconditional","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 10.5 (The upper (carries) successor needs no exceptional-cell exclusion)","locator":"Long record Proposition 10.5, p. 115, label prop:upper-unconditional","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $s\\ge5$ and suppose the upper branch occurs at row $s$, that is, the transition at row $s$ is on branch $\\mathrm U$ of Theorem 5.16. Then\n$$\n\\mathrm{rem}(s+1)\\le2^{s+1}.\n$$\nIndeed, the reset identity expresses $2^{s+1}$ as $\\mathrm{rem}(s+1)$ plus a nonnegative reset charge. Thus the upper branch needs no exceptional-value exclusion for the next-row two-sided invariant. This conclusion concerns that induction step, not the absence of upper transitions on the orbit.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-upper-unconditional","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.prop-upper-unconditional","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-upper-unconditional%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_upper_branch_needs_no_exceptional_cell%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.prop-upper-unconditional%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_upper_branch_needs_no_exceptional_cell%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_upper_branch_needs_no_